course: dictionary
lesson: 11882
title: Breadth: width and more
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Breadth is how wide something is, from one side to the other. Length is how long something is, and breadth is how wide it is. «The rug is 3 metres long and 2 metres in breadth.»
explain: In maths, breadth is another word for width. To find the area of a rectangle, multiply the length by the breadth. «A rectangle is 6 cm long and has a breadth of 4 cm, so its area is 24 square centimetres.»
explain: Breadth can also mean how many different things something covers. «Her breadth of knowledge impressed everyone: she knew about space, music and history.» And «by a hair's breadth» means only just, by a tiny amount. «The cup missed the floor by a hair's breadth.»
fact: Breadth means width: how far something is from side to side.
fact: Length is how long something is, and breadth is how wide it is.
fact: Area of a rectangle = length × breadth.
fact: «Breadth of knowledge» means knowing many different things.
fact: «By a hair's breadth» means only just, by a tiny amount.
exercise: «The river was ten metres in breadth.» What does breadth mean here? | The colour of the water | The depth of the water under the boat | *The width of the river from bank to bank | The length of the river from its source
exercise: «The rectangle has a length of 8 cm and a breadth of 3 cm.» What is its area? | 16 square cm | *24 square cm | 11 square cm | 3 square cm
exercise: «He escaped the falling rock by a hair's breadth.» What does this phrase mean? | Far away from the rock | *Only just, by a tiny amount | With a big cut on his hand | After a very long time
test: «Her breadth of knowledge impressed the teachers.» What does breadth of knowledge mean? | Knowing one thing very deeply and nothing else | Writing in very large letters | *Knowing many different things | Reading very fast
test: Which word means how wide something is, from side to side? | Length | Depth | *Breadth | Height
exam: «The school report praised the breadth of the curriculum, with many subjects taught.» What does breadth of the curriculum mean? | *Many different subjects | One short lesson | The size of the classroom | Long hours of sport
